questions.detailed_answer:
i) semilogx:
- Plots data with the x-axis on a logarithmic scale and y-axis on a linear scale.
- Useful for frequency response, signal processing, wide-range x data.
- Syntax: semilogx(x, y)
- Example:
  x = [1 10 100 1000];
  y = [0 1 2 3];
  semilogx(x, y, 'b-o');
  xlabel('log scale x'); ylabel('y'); title('semilogx example');

ii) errorbar:
- Plots data points with error bars (vertical by default).
- Shows uncertainty or variation in measurements.
- Syntax: errorbar(x, y, err)        % symmetric error
         errorbar(x, y, neg, pos)   % asymmetric error
- Example:
  x = 1:5;
  y = [2 4 3 5 4];
  err = [0.1 0.2 0.15 0.1 0.2];
  errorbar(x, y, err);
  title('Measurement with error bars');

iii) fplot:
- Automatically evaluates and plots a function without manually creating x vector.
- Adaptively samples more points where the function changes rapidly.
- Syntax: fplot(f)                  % plot over [-5, 5] by default
         fplot(f, [xmin xmax])     % over specified range
         fplot(@(x) sin(x), [0 2*pi]);
- Example:
  fplot(@(x) x.^2 - 3*x + 2, [-1 4]);
  grid on; title('Quadratic function');

questions.matlab:
% i) semilogx
figure(1);
x = [1 10 100 1000 10000];  % wide range x
y = log10(x);                % corresponding y
semilogx(x, y, 'b-o');      % log x-axis
title('semilogx example'); grid on;

% ii) errorbar
figure(2);
x2 = 1:5;
y2 = [2 4 3 5 4];            % data
err = [0.2 0.3 0.2 0.1 0.25]; % error values
errorbar(x2, y2, err);        % plot with error bars
title('errorbar example'); grid on;

% iii) fplot
figure(3);
fplot(@(x) x.^2 - 3*x + 2, [-1 4]);  % plot function over range
title('fplot example'); grid on;

% Parametric plot
t = linspace(0, 2*pi, 1000);  % parameter t from 0 to 2pi

% Compute parametric coordinates
x = cos(t).^3;    % x = cos^3(t)
y = sin(t).^3;    % y = sin^3(t)
u = cos(t);       % u = cos(t)
v = sin(t);       % v = sin(t)

% Plot both curves in one figure
figure;
plot(x, y, 'b-', 'LineWidth', 2);  % plot astroid
hold on;
plot(u, v, 'r--', 'LineWidth', 2); % plot unit circle

axis([-2 2 -2 2]);    % set axis range -2 to 2
xlabel('x / u'); ylabel('y / v');
title('Parametric Curves');
legend('y=sin^3(t) vs x=cos^3(t)', 'v=cos(t) vs u=sin(t)');
grid on;

% Corrected code
x = [20, 25];        % x data points
y = [100, 120];      % y data points
y1 = 112;            % query value

% interp1(y, x, y1, method) finds x given y
x1 = interp1(y, x, y1, 'nearest');  % nearest neighbor
x2 = interp1(y, x, y1, 'linear');   % linear interpolation (corrected from 'Linear')
x3 = interp1(y, x, y1, 'spline');   % spline interpolation
x4 = interp1(y, x, y1, 'pchip');    % piecewise cubic hermite (variable renamed to x4)

fprintf('Nearest: x1 = %.4f\n', x1);
fprintf('Linear:  x2 = %.4f\n', x2);
fprintf('Spline:  x3 = %.4f\n', x3);
fprintf('Pchip:   x4 = %.4f\n', x4);

% if-elseif-else-end example: Grade classification
score = 75;                  % student score

if score >= 90               % check for A grade
    grade = 'A';
elseif score >= 80           % check for B grade
    grade = 'B';
elseif score >= 70           % check for C grade
    grade = 'C';
elseif score >= 60           % check for D grade
    grade = 'D';
else                         % all others fail
    grade = 'F';
end

fprintf('Score: %d, Grade: %s\n', score, grade);
